# The sum of two texts is a rope. It is made flat once, ahead of the loop, and there its characters, length and width are read, once each.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="checksum" role=Source
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[rope]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}:Add)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[word]] = Load(b@[[rope]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:JSRopeString_fiber0, {{*}}:FlattenString)
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:JSRopeString_fiber0
# CHECK: Load(b@[[header]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:StringImpl_data, {{*}}:FlattenString)
# CHECK-NEXT: Load(b@[[header]], offset = 4, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:StringImpl_length, {{*}}:FlattenString)
# CHECK-NEXT: Load(b@[[header]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:StringImpl_hashAndFlags, {{*}}:FlattenString)
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:StringImpl
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# No loop asks again whether the text is a rope, and none calls.
# HOT-LABEL: name="checksum" role=Source
# HOT-NOT: Reads:JSRopeString
# HOT-NOT: Reads:StringImpl
# HOT-NOT: ExitsSideways
# HOT-LABEL: end of function
# CALLS-LABEL: f3: size=
# CALLS-NEXT: stub Concatenate.n2 x1
# CALLS-NEXT: stub FlattenString x1
# CALLS-NEXT: f4: size=
